(6776830, 1015630, 59695, '<td valign="top">I liked the creativity (not a stock flower or landscape), the humour, the textures and details.<br/>How anyone could vote less than 5 is beyond me and the two 1''s it can only be tactical voting, or a poor judge because how do they vore for the poorly composed, focused, lit, exposed shots!? - it was a 7 from me.</td>', 'I liked the creativity (not a stock flower or landscape), the humour, the textures and details.How anyone could vote less than 5 is beyond me and the two 1''s it can only be tactical voting, or a poor judge because how do they vore for the poorly composed, focused, lit, exposed shots!? - it was a 7 from me.', '2012-05-23 18:05:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6776837, 1015217, 103142, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aliqui:</b></div><hr/><i> It''s a great scene, but honestly the blown highlights detract from the scene for me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I do agree -- however it''s a very difficult area to shoot. The birds are actually quite dark, so you need to overexpose to get the details in the shadows. Even though I shoot RAW, when it''s bright sunlight, you either lose the shadows or over expose the head/wing tops. Too bad it can''t shoot fast enough to bracket while flying! :)<br/> <br/>You''re at the mercy of the light.</td>', 'Originally posted by aliqui: It''s a great scene, but honestly the blown highlights detract from the scene for me.   I do agree -- however it''s a very difficult area to shoot. The birds are actually quite dark, so you need to overexpose to get the details in the shadows. Even though I shoot RAW, when it''s bright sunlight, you either lose the shadows or over expose the head/wing tops. Too bad it can''t shoot fast enough to bracket while flying! :) You''re at the mercy of the light.', '2012-05-23 18:26:18.000000', NULL, 0),
