(6778203, 1015630, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nodster:</b></div><hr/><i>How anyone could vote less than 5 is beyond me and the two 1''s it can only be tactical voting, or a poor judge...</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I donno about that. I''m surprised, personally, it didn''t get MORE lowball votes. I mean, from one perspective it''s an underexposed snapshot of three chicken butts, and this isn''t what many people are looking for when they think of "spring" :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by nodster:How anyone could vote less than 5 is beyond me and the two 1''s it can only be tactical voting, or a poor judge...  I donno about that. I''m surprised, personally, it didn''t get MORE lowball votes. I mean, from one perspective it''s an underexposed snapshot of three chicken butts, and this isn''t what many people are looking for when they think of "spring" :-)', '2012-05-25 11:33:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778229, 1015337, 113900, '<td valign="top">This is a very nice shot.  It''s clear and sharp and the colors are great.<br/> <br/>Now, here''s some advice in terms of DPC.<br/> <br/>A similar shot that would score higher on DPC would be a tighter shot on the elk.  Zoom in and use a large aperture to create nice bokeh.  You might have been all the way zoomed in anyway, I understand.  Also, a slightly different angle with the Elk''s head not directly in front of the big tree in the background may have allowed you to crop in tighter on the elk''s head.<br/> <br/>Don''t take this as criticism of the original image because it''s not, I personally like it a lot.  Just some DPC score related advice for you.</td>', 'This is a very nice shot.  It''s clear and sharp and the colors are great. Now, here''s some advice in terms of DPC. A similar shot that would score higher on DPC would be a tighter shot on the elk.  Zoom in and use a large aperture to create nice bokeh.  You might have been all the way zoomed in anyway, I understand.  Also, a slightly different angle with the Elk''s head not directly in front of the big tree in the background may have allowed you to crop in tighter on the elk''s head. Don''t take this as criticism of the original image because it''s not, I personally like it a lot.  Just some DPC score related advice for you.', '2012-05-25 12:05:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778252, 1015679, 12611, '<td valign="top">great tones. vive la minimalism!</td>', 'great tones. vive la minimalism!', '2012-05-25 12:33:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778426, 1015701, 94265, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skewsme:</b></div><hr/><i> wow, stunning!  what a refreshing and crazy portrait, great model!  only suggestion I have is to smooth out the wrinkles in her shirt and skirt so that they don''t distract.  make this lady a star! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you, the camera definitely loves her, she has a unique style. :-) I prefer to keep details like creases etc. though as I think it looks a bit unnatural without them. I liked the flamingoes on her skirt, apparently it was a gift from a designer whom she has modelled for!</td>', 'Originally posted by skewsme: wow, stunning!  what a refreshing and crazy portrait, great model!  only suggestion I have is to smooth out the wrinkles in her shirt and skirt so that they don''t distract.  make this lady a star!   Thank you, the camera definitely loves her, she has a unique style. :-) I prefer to keep details like creases etc. though as I think it looks a bit unnatural without them. I liked the flamingoes on her skirt, apparently it was a gift from a designer whom she has modelled for!', '2012-05-25 17:14:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778479, 1015276, 37252, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this challenge, but had I voted I would have given this a 5. I like the quirky head tilt of the chick and the DOF. I wish the feet were not cropped off and that the image wasn''t so dark.</td>', 'I didn''t vote on this challenge, but had I voted I would have given this a 5. I like the quirky head tilt of the chick and the DOF. I wish the feet were not cropped off and that the image wasn''t so dark.', '2012-05-25 18:48:15.000000', NULL, 0),
