(6778647, 1015793, 124815, '<td valign="top">I gave it a 9 and forgot to bump it to 10 - in case you look at marks.<br/>I looked at the picture and loved it and recognized your hand and wondered how you did it again.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=951465" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1391/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_951465.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1391/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_951465.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1391/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_951465.jpg"/></a> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=985761" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1487/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_985761.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1487/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_985761.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1487/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_985761.jpg"/></a> <br/>Are they all taken with your macro lens Canon EF 100mm f/2.8L Macro IS USM ?</td>', 'I gave it a 9 and forgot to bump it to 10 - in case you look at marks.I looked at the picture and loved it and recognized your hand and wondered how you did it again.  Are they all taken with your macro lens Canon EF 100mm f/2.8L Macro IS USM ?', '2012-05-25 22:57:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778677, 1015793, 54645, '<td valign="top">Thank you Mariuca. Yes, all with the 100mm f/2.8L. For some reason I enjoy shooting poppies which usually requires getting down amongst the plants and flowers. The bokeh with this lens is very appealing, and you can see it when shooting, thus it''s not too difficult to create interesting backgrounds with shapes and light. Set it to manual focus and waver about until the world looks groovy. :)</td>', 'Thank you Mariuca. Yes, all with the 100mm f/2.8L. For some reason I enjoy shooting poppies which usually requires getting down amongst the plants and flowers. The bokeh with this lens is very appealing, and you can see it when shooting, thus it''s not too difficult to create interesting backgrounds with shapes and light. Set it to manual focus and waver about until the world looks groovy. :)', '2012-05-25 23:52:55.000000', NULL, 0),
